  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Favorable Opportunity For Self-Advancement of Today&#x2019;s Youth Plus Activity (FORSATY Plus)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of FORSATY Plus is to strengthen protective factors to Violent Extremism (VE) and provide positive pathways for youth and community development in Morocco to reduce individual vulnerabilities to VE and build resilience in marginalized persons. The Activity also seeks to increase the capacity of the Government of Morocco (GoM) and other Moroccan institutions and communities to sustain and replicate successful preventing/countering violent extremism (P/CVE) models and use monitoring, evaluation and learning (MEL) methods. FORSATY Plus framework is composed of three main outcomes that drive the program, and one cross-cutting outcome than brings value to and builds synergies between the three operational outcomes: Outcome 1: Moroccan public institutions apply improved models and MEL methods. Outcome 2: Civil society sustainably assumes a larger role in building individual resilience&#x2022;Outcome 3: Moroccan communities acquire local ownership and increase their resilience&#x2022;Cross-cutting outcome: FORSATY Plus interventions adopt a holistic approach and thrive on intersectoral collaboration.</narrative>
  </description>
